{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-317329",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5a\\cdot ((6b)\\times (4c)) & =120 \\\\ (-5)\\cdot 6\\cdot 4\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =120 \\\\ (-120)[a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =120 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
